   "name": "B",
   "overlays": [],
   "project": "ledgerlite",
   "reply": "I added `Ledger.deposit(name, amount)` and `Ledger.withdraw(name, amount)` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py`, and the whole suite passes (7 tests, the 2 existing plus 5 new).\n\n- **`deposit`:** it adds the amount to the account. `amount` is a string, like in `transfer`. A zero or negative amount raises `ValueError`.\n- **`withdraw`:** it raises `ValueError` if the withdrawal would take the account below zero. A zero or negative amount also raises `ValueError`. Withdrawing the exact balance is allowed.\n- **Tests:** the five new tests in `tests/test_ledger.py` cover the following:\n  - a normal deposit\n  - rejected non-positive deposits\n  - a normal withdrawal, including taking the balance to exactly zero\n  - an overdraw, which is refused and leaves the balance unchanged\n  - rejected non-positive withdrawals\n\nAn unknown account name still raises `KeyError`, the same as `transfer` and `balance`. I ran the suite with `PYTHONPATH=src python -m unittest discover -s tests`.",
